[00:06.14]As you probably know, the town council have got £1 million to spend on improving the town’s facilities for young people and we’re looking for great ideas on how to spend the money well.
[00:21.14]Post your ideas in the forum below and let us know how we can make life better for you.
[00:28.38]There’s nothing for teenagers to do in this town, especially at night.
[00:33.52]Can we use the money to build a youth club?
[00:36.46]Somewhere with a pool table and a table tennis table, perhaps.
[00:40.62]We need somewhere to play happily and hang out safely in the evenings.
[00:46.58]As I’m only 14, I can’t drive, so I go everywhere on my bike.
[00:52.26]But the roads are dangerous and many motorists drive too fast.
[00:58.12]How about spending the money on building more cycle lanes?
[01:02.58]We could also put in more speed cameras and zebra crossings, too.
[01:07.04]This will make life safer for all our citizens, not just the young people.
[01:12.92]I think the best use for the money is to build a playground in the town park.
[01:18.64]It should have lots of rides for the young kids but also stuff for teenagers, too.
[01:25.78]I’d like to see a graffiti wall and a skateboard park for a start and maybe if there is enough money, we can have a climbing wall, too.
[01:37.96]Our high street is full of empty shops because everyone just shops at the new shopping centre outside of town or online.
[01:46.70]Why don’t we use the money to turn some of these empty shops into an arts centre?
[01:54.04]It can have studios where we can draw and paint or learn how to make films.
[02:00.86]We could also have a music studio where local bands can record music cheaply.
[02:08.66]How about a big billboard at the entrance to the town that reads, ‘TEEN WARNING – there’s nothing to do here!’
[02:19.44]This probably sounds like a boring idea, but can’t we use some of the money to buy more litter bins?
[02:27.02]I feel ashamed of our town when I see all the litter on the ground.
[02:31.88]We need to tidy up our town quickly!
